<title>UK: Goode Durrant shares up on H1 results.</title>
<headline>Goode Durrant shares up on H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Goode Durrant Plc, a specialist vehicle and equipment hire group, rose on Thursday after the company released improved interim results and expressed optimism about 1997.</p>
<p>By 0925 GMT the shares were up 13p at 421-1/2p in trading volume of 42,500 shares.</p>
<p>The group's pretax profit for the six months ended 31 October 1996 rose 13 percent to 15.2 million stg, while the dividend was increased by 14 percent to 3.2p.</p>
<p>The group said it was &quot;encouraged about the prospects for the current financial year and for 1997 as a whole.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7945</p>
